From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] apklayer: SettingsProvider: SSAID lookup keyed by the package uid

The lookup used the caller uid (99000+ for an isolated process) but generateSsaidLocked stores under the
app uid: once the entry existed, a second request regenerated the value, insertSettingLocked changed
nothing and "Ssaid settings not accessible" was thrown. Key both by callingPkg.applicationInfo.uid.
Against frameworks/base 653be4a9d2b0 (REVISION). Apply: patches/apply aosp <LineageOS tree>.
---
diff --git a/packages/SettingsProvider/src/com/android/providers/settings/SettingsProvider.java b/packages/SettingsProvider/src/com/android/providers/settings/SettingsProvider.java
index 8ddd1673ea15..730608a51be0 100644
--- a/packages/SettingsProvider/src/com/android/providers/settings/SettingsProvider.java
+++ b/packages/SettingsProvider/src/com/android/providers/settings/SettingsProvider.java
@@ -1823,8 +1823,8 @@ public class SettingsProvider extends ContentProvider {
     @GuardedBy("mLock")
     private Setting getSsaidSettingLocked(PackageInfo callingPkg, int owningUserId) {
         // Get uid of caller (key) used to store ssaid value
-        String name = Integer.toString(
-                UserHandle.getUid(owningUserId, UserHandle.getAppId(Binder.getCallingUid())));
+        // apklayer patch: the app's uid, the key generateSsaidLocked stores under; an isolated process (uid 99000+) would look up another key
+        String name = Integer.toString(callingPkg.applicationInfo.uid);
 
         if (DEBUG) {
             Slog.v(LOG_TAG, "getSsaidSettingLocked(" + name + "," + owningUserId + ")");
